From 4ffc10e143a9b77d5103bcb95f99d46f337c4d72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:49:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent: default Claude agents prefer the system adapter over
 npm

Patch 0033 made Claude Agent (Plus) and Claude Agent TUI default agents, but
always launched them through `npm install <package>@latest` -- even on a
Gentoo system where the claude-agent-acp-plus / claude-agent-acp-tui USE flags
had already installed the Portage-built adapter under /usr/bin. The installed
binary was dead weight, the version that ran was whatever npm published last
(no release-age cooldown), and the ebuilds still asked for hand-written
agent_servers entries duplicating the defaults. Story 019, 2026-10-07.

The rule: on every start of one of the two Zeo ids, run the system binary when
it exists and is executable, npm otherwise.

  agent_registry_store.rs adds zeo_agent_launch_source(id, probe), a pure
  resolver: claude-agent-acp-plus -> /usr/bin/claude-agent-acp-plus,
  claude-agent-tui -> /usr/bin/claude-agent-acp-tui (the TUI id and its
  binary name differ; tests pin both directions). Ok(true) gives the system
  path; Ok(false) or any probe error gives 0033's npm spec; any other id
  gets npm without a probe. The production probe,
  zeo_system_binary_is_executable, follows symlinks (npm installs bins as
  symlinks) and wants a regular file with an executable bit; a missing path
  or a dangling symlink is Ok(false), so a zeo-bin user without the adapter
  sees no warning on every start.

  agent_server_store.rs gives LocalRegistryNpxAgent a launch_probe and
  consults it in get_command, once per start -- installing or removing the
  adapter takes effect on the next thread with no rebuild. The system branch
  returns the absolute binary with the registry args, Zed's extra args and
  env, and no node and no npm install; the npm branch is unchanged. Every
  launch logs one line, `zeo agent launch: agent_id=... source=system
  path=...` or `source=npm package=...`; a probe error logs at WARN with the
  agent id and falls back.

Absolute paths, never a bare name: a bare command depends on the spawn-time
PATH. The decision is at launch time, not build time, because zeo-bin is
built once for every user and cannot read USE flags; the same code serves
app-editors/zeo (binary present whenever its USE flag is on) and zeo-bin
(present only if the user installed the adapter). Inside the Flatpak the
host's /usr/bin is not visible, so it takes the npm path by construction.

What is unchanged: the agent ids (0036 stores thread configuration per id),
and the settings merge -- a user agent_servers entry with the same id
replaces the default and is never resolved through this rule. default.json's
comment now says the system adapter is tried first.

Tests: the resolver's hostile cases (look-alike ids, the TUI name mismatch,
probe errors), the production probe against a non-executable file, a
directory, a missing path, a dangling symlink, an executable and a symlink to
one; get_command keeps npm for other registry agents, rechecks every start,
and launches the system binary without preparing an npm install; with
default.json both defaults resolve the system binary and a user entry of the
same id wins.
